---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import data from '../../../data/hkipoblindbox.json';
import binary from '../../../data/hkipoblindbox-binary.json';
const h = data.historical;
const pct = (v: number) => `${(v * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
const bands = ['Below 0%', '0–<20%', '20–<40%', '40% or more'];
const lenses = [
  ['天时', 'Timing', 'Why this industry, now?'],
  ['地利', 'Position', 'What advantage can survive competition?'],
  ['人和', 'People', 'Who runs it, and whose interests come first?'],
  ['验货', 'Proof', 'Show the product, customers and cash.'],
  ['价格', 'Valuation', 'A small share price can hide a large price tag.'],
  ['场势', 'Market setup', 'Who can buy, who can sell, and when?'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="The HK IPO Blind Box — Joy — Robin Xie" description="One human, one AI, and an allocation algorithm with no sense of humor. A public, simulated Hong Kong IPO prediction experiment." path="/binary/joy/hkipoblindbox/" schema={[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"The HK IPO Blind Box","description":"An auditable simulated Hong Kong IPO prediction experiment.","url":"https://iamrobin.ai/binary/joy/hkipoblindbox/","datePublished":"2026-09-21","author":{"@id":"https://www.tideisun.com/robin#robin-xie"}}]}>
  <article class="blindbox">
    <a class="back" href="/binary/#binary-lane-joy">← Binary / Blog / Joy</a>
    <header class="hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">JOY FIELD NOTES · EXPERIMENT 001</p>
        <h1>The HK IPO<br/><em>Blind Box.</em></h1>
        <p class="deck">I researched the company.<br/>The allocation algorithm researched my patience.</p>
        <p class="intro">One human. One AI. Six serious questions.<br/>An unreasonable amount of joy about possibly receiving nothing.</p>
        <div class="badges"><span>Simulated money only</span><span>Forecasts frozen first</span></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="box-figure" aria-label="A sealed blind box: the answer belongs to the future">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 400 370" role="img" aria-labelledby="box-title">
          <title id="box-title">A sealed IPO blind box awaiting reality</title>
          <ellipse cx="205" cy="306" rx="135" ry="18" fill="#746d65" opacity=".08"/>
          <path d="M80 134 210 75 337 139 207 203Z" fill="#f7eee3" stroke="#a38e70" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <path d="M80 134 207 203 207 319 80 247Z" fill="#e4d9c9" stroke="#a38e70" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <path d="M207 203 337 139 337 251 207 319Z" fill="#f1e8db" stroke="#a38e70" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <path d="M136 108 265 172 286 162 159 97Z" fill="#dfb7c4" opacity=".9"/>
          <path d="M265 172 286 162 286 211 265 222Z" fill="#d5a6b5"/>
          <text x="246" y="265" fill="#8b6b47" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="58" transform="rotate(-26 246 265)">?</text>
          <text x="39" y="42" fill="#746d65" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" letter-spacing="2">CONTENTS: UNKNOWN</text>
          <path d="M148 46 Q191 35 218 57" fill="none" stroke="#b4915d" stroke-dasharray="3 5"/>
          <circle cx="341" cy="62" r="4" fill="#dfb7c4"/><path d="M43 213h16m-8-8v16" stroke="#b4915d"/>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>Research inside. Certainty sold separately.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <section class="story" aria-labelledby="story-title">
      <span class="section-no">01 / THE PLOT</span>
      <h2 id="story-title">An investment committee walks into a toy shop.</h2>
      <div class="story-columns">
        <p>It began with IPO notices, company research, and increasingly elaborate conversations about robots. Soon we had six lenses, a LABUBU on the committee, and a theory about lucky stock-code digits. The company name occasionally achieved escape velocity before its business model did.</p>
        <p>This experiment keeps the jokes and puts the predictions on the record. We make a dated guess, seal it, and let the first three trading days answer. Every miss stays visible. Personal accounts and the private research machinery stay behind the curtain.</p>
      </div>
      <blockquote>“We researched like an investment committee.<br/>We waited like children outside a toy shop.”</blockquote>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="lenses-title">
      <span class="section-no">02 / SIX QUESTIONS BEFORE OPENING</span>
      <h2 id="lenses-title">Curiosity, with a checklist.</h2>
      <div class="lenses">{lenses.map(([han, en, question]) => <div class="lens"><span lang="zh">{han}</span><h3>{en}</h3><p>{question}</p></div>)}</div>
      <p class="aside">Names, lucky 6s and 8s, and cheap-looking tickets belong in the hypothesis notebook. They have not earned a predictive edge.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="executive" aria-labelledby="binary-title">
      <span class="section-no">THE HUMAN BUTTON · FIVE TRADING SESSIONS</span>
      <h2 id="binary-title">Will the box pay for its own confetti?</h2>
      <p>Robin requested one button: <strong>if allotted, do we predict a +10% limit sell within the first five trading sessions?</strong> The answer is YES or NO. The allocation algorithm already supplies enough rejection.</p>
      <p class="aside">YES is a frozen forecast, not a promised fill. Default participation is SUBSCRIBE unless the registered screen finds a serious reason to skip. A NO forecast alone does not veto a box. This separate layer has no demonstrated forward edge yet.</p>
      <div class="binary-list">{binary.forecasts.map((f) => <article class="binary-card">
        <header><span class="ticker">HKEX · {f.stock_code}</span><h3>{f.issuer_name}</h3></header>
        <div class="binary-answer"><strong>{f.prediction}</strong><span>+10% by session five?</span></div>
        <p class="participation">{f.participation} · simulated participation</p>
        <p>Conditional sell limit: <strong>{f.target_at_offer_low && f.target_at_offer_low !== f.target_at_offer_high ? `HK$${f.target_at_offer_low.toFixed(2)}–${f.target_at_offer_high.toFixed(2)}` : `HK$${f.target_at_offer_high.toFixed(2)}`}</strong></p>
        <p class="aside">Based on {f.offer_low && f.offer_low !== f.offer_high ? `HK$${f.offer_low.toFixed(2)}–${f.offer_high.toFixed(2)}` : `HK$${f.offer_high.toFixed(2)}`} offer terms; recompute from the final issue price, rounding up to a valid tick.</p>
        <details><summary>The sealed receipt</summary><p>Frozen {f.frozen_at}<br/>Version {f.version}<br/>Expected listing {f.listing_date}</p><code>{f.commitment}</code><a href={f.prospectus_url}>Issuer prospectus ↗</a></details>
      </article>)}</div>
      <p><strong>The exit rule:</strong> keep the +10% limit through sessions 1–5. From session 6, use an OCO +10% target / −10% stop. A gap below the stop can lose more than 10%. A price touching a limit does not prove an order filled.</p>
      <blockquote>“The lottery handles rejection.<br/>We handle the receipts.”</blockquote>
      <details><summary>The five-day rehearsal, with the awkward bits left in</summary><p>The {binary.historical.window[0]}–{binary.historical.window[1]} inventory contains {binary.historical.inventory} listings. Under the declared daily-bar execution assumptions, {binary.historical.yes_d5} of {binary.historical.known_d5} resolved five-day labels reached the +10% limit in time; {binary.historical.no_d5} did not. One recent listing is still pending. This is historical reconstruction, not unseen prediction or a personal trading win rate.</p><p>The binary prediction recipe scored {pct(binary.historical.binary_accuracy)}, versus {pct(binary.historical.always_yes_accuracy)} for always saying YES. The fixed screen excluded no IPOs, so it selected the same portfolio as subscribing to all. No screening advantage has been demonstrated. There are {binary.historical.modeled_exits} modeled exits, {binary.historical.execution_gaps} unresolved execution histories, and {binary.historical.open_positions} known open positions. Missing evidence stays missing; we do not publish a complete portfolio return from an incomplete ledger.</p><p>Only redacted calls and aggregate evidence appear here. Private model details, capital assumptions and personal logs remain private.</p></details>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="forward-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-no">03 / SEALED ENVELOPES</span><h2 id="forward-title">The next boxes.</h2></div><span class="pending">{data.forecasts.length} frozen · outcomes pending</span></div>
      <p class="section-intro">These are forecasts for the highest traded price within the first three trading days, relative to the final issue price. The initial probabilities are <strong>uncalibrated research priors</strong>. There is no earned forward win rate yet.</p>
      <details class="legacy"><summary>Open the original three-session research (unchanged)</summary>
      <div class="forecast-list">{data.forecasts.map((f) => <article class="forecast">
        <header><span class="ticker">HKEX · {f.stock_code}</span><h3>{f.issuer_name}</h3><p>Expected listing · <time datetime={f.listing_date ?? ''}>{f.listing_date}</time></p></header>
        <div class="probabilities" aria-label="Frozen return probabilities">{f.probabilities.map((p,i) => <div><span>{bands[i]}</span><strong>{pct(p)}</strong><i style={`--prob:${p * 100}%`} aria-hidden="true"></i></div>)}</div>
        <footer><p>Comparison sell target: <strong>final issue price × {(1+f.target_return).toFixed(2)}</strong>. Price touching the target does not prove an order filled.</p><details><summary>Open the timestamp, not the box</summary><p>Frozen {f.frozen_at}<br/>Version {f.model_version}</p><code>{f.commitment}</code></details></footer>
      </article>)}</div></details>
    </section>

    <section class="history" aria-labelledby="history-title">
      <span class="section-no">04 / THE REHEARSAL</span>
      <h2 id="history-title">History has already read the ending.</h2>
      <p>The 24-month reconstruction runs from {h.window[0]} to {h.window[1]}. It uses dated offering evidence and chronological evaluation. It remains a reconstruction; these are not unseen forward wins.</p>
      <div class="numbers"><div><strong>{h.eligible}</strong><span>eligible IPOs inventoried</span></div><div><strong>{h.scored}</strong><span>three-day outcomes scored</span></div><div><strong>{h.missing}</strong><span>explicit data gaps</span></div><div><strong>{pct(h.assessment.accuracy)}</strong><span>exact class accuracy · final {h.assessment.n} cases</span></div></div>
      <p class="aside">Assessment 95% interval: {pct(h.assessment.wilson95[0])}–{pct(h.assessment.wilson95[1])}. Multiclass Brier score: {h.assessment.brier.toFixed(3)} (lower is better). The baseline survived the predeclared validation gate. A more complicated story has to earn its place.</p>
      <details><summary>What this score means</summary><p>Accuracy asks whether the highest three-day return landed in the predicted band. Direction, distance, probability error and target touches are scored separately. Missing data never becomes a loss, a win or a zero. The historical label coverage is incomplete and may be selective.</p><p>{h.data_note} Trading costs and allocation uncertainty are separate from price prediction. Quarterly reviews may introduce a new model version; they cannot revise old answers.</p></details>
    </section>

    <section class="letter"><span class="section-no">05 / TO FUTURE ROBIN</span><h2>Keep the curiosity.<br/><em>Keep the receipts.</em></h2><p>A robot can refuse to pick us. A stock can refuse to rise. We can still leave behind an honest record of how we thought—and how much we laughed.</p><p class="rule">Bubu can guess wrong. Bubu cannot secretly edit the exam paper.</p></section>
    <footer class="page-notes"><p>Public snapshot · {binary.generated_at.slice(0,10)} · Simulated experiment<br/>Sources: <a href="https://www2.hkexnews.hk/New-Listings/New-Listing-Information/Main-Board?sc_lang=en">HKEX offering documents</a> and archived daily-price evidence.</p><a href="/binary/#binary-lane-joy">Return to Joy ↗</a></footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .blindbox{width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 48px));margin:50px auto 0}.back{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:30px;align-items:center;padding:70px 0 65px}.eyebrow,.section-no{font:10px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--gold-dark)}h1{font:clamp(52px,6.8vw,88px)/1.02 var(--serif);letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:24px 0}h1 em,h2 em{font-weight:400;color:var(--gold-dark)}.deck{font:22px/1.45 var(--serif);margin:24px 0}.intro{font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}.badges{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:28px}.badges span,.pending{font:10px var(--mono);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:9px 11px;border-radius:20px}.box-figure{margin:0}.box-figure svg{width:100%;height:auto}.box-figure figcaption{text-align:center;font:italic 14px var(--serif);color:var(--muted)}section{padding:60px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}h2{font:clamp(30px,4vw,45px)/1.15 var(--serif);letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:16px 0 28px}.story-columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px}.story p,section>p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted)}blockquote{font:italic 26px/1.5 var(--serif);margin:25px 0 0;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--gold-dark)}.lenses{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:26px 35px}.lens{padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.lens>span{font:26px var(--serif);color:var(--gold-dark)}.lens h3{font-size:13px;margin:12px 0 8px}.lens p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);margin:0}.aside{font-size:12px!important;line-height:1.8!important;margin:20px 0 0}.section-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center}.pending{white-space:nowrap;background:#edf0e8}.section-intro{max-width:760px}.forecast-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px;margin-top:30px}.forecast{padding:26px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;background:rgba(253,251,247,.55)}.ticker{font:10px var(--mono);color:var(--gold-dark);letter-spacing:.07em}.forecast h3{font:23px/1.25 var(--serif);margin:12px 0;min-height:58px}.forecast header p{font:11px var(--mono);color:var(--muted)}.probabilities{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;padding:20px 0}.probabilities div{position:relative;padding-bottom:12px}.probabilities span{display:block;font-size:10px;color:var(--muted)}.probabilities strong{font:23px var(--serif);display:block;margin-top:5px}.probabilities i{position:absolute;bottom:0;height:3px;left:0;width:var(--prob);background:var(--gold)}.forecast footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:15px;font-size:11px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted)}details{margin-top:16px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink)}code{display:block;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:9px}.numbers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:24px;margin:32px 0}.numbers strong{font:48px var(--serif);display:block;letter-spacing:-.04em}.numbers span{display:block;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;max-width:145px;margin-top:8px}.letter{max-width:700px}.letter h2{font-size:50px}.rule{color:var(--ink)!important;font:italic 19px/1.5 var(--serif)!important}.page-notes{display:flex;gap:24px;justify-content:space-between;padding:25px 0 60px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:11px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}
  .binary-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;margin-top:30px}.binary-card{padding:26px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:rgba(253,251,247,.55)}.binary-card h3{font:22px/1.3 var(--serif);margin:12px 0;min-height:58px}.binary-card p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}.binary-answer{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px;margin:24px 0 12px}.binary-answer strong{font:52px var(--serif);color:#536047}.binary-answer span{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}.binary-card .participation{font:11px var(--mono);color:var(--ink)}.legacy>summary{padding:18px 0;font-size:14px}
  @media(max-width:700px){.binary-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}.binary-card h3{min-height:0}}
  @media(max-width:700px){.blindbox{width:calc(100% - 36px);margin-top:28px}.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:45px 0;gap:10px}.box-figure{width:78%;margin:0 auto}.story-columns,.forecast-list{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:15px}.lenses{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px 22px}.section-heading{display:block}.pending{display:inline-block;margin-bottom:20px}.numbers{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:25px}.numbers strong{font-size:44px}section{padding:42px 0}.forecast h3{min-height:0}.page-notes{display:block}.letter h2{font-size:42px}blockquote{font-size:23px}}
</style>
